      "id": "ex:msyn/10.1021-ja01629a058/claim/copper-gasket-dissolved",
      "label": "Claim",
      "props": {
        "name": "0.1 to 0.2 g of the copper gasket dissolved and deposited as metallic copper",
        "claim_kind": "finding",
        "claim_status": "supported",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "locator": "p. 2",
            "note": "quote withheld: sha256:bff961297f21ba711e9ecc0d7e045fb99191e8418e4ac140c47a06f331a7b76f chars:105",
            "source": "ex:msyn/source/10.1021-ja01629a058"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "locator": "p. 2",
            "note": "quote withheld: sha256:907e16f8284cf47ae9684ad4992e051755689640a885c18826d7dd8d09efc096 chars:105",
            "passage": "10.1021-ja01629a058/p2/1",
            "source": "ex:msyn/source/10.1021-ja01629a058"
          }
        ],
        "inference_type": "observational",
        "statement": "In each oxo reaction 0.1 to 0.2 g of the copper gasket dissolved and deposited as metallic copper in the top of the autoclave; some of the oxo reactions went more slowly."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ex:msyn/10.1021-ja01629a058/claim/possible-acetic-acid-artifact",
      "label": "Claim",
      "props": {
        "name": "oxidation of the n-propyl alcohol may have yielded some acetic acid",
        "claim_kind": "data_quality",
        "claim_status": "proposed",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "locator": "p. 2",
            "note": "quote withheld: sha256:b6a28d29b04038b499315f884c8729e19778306c546c81c93b5e9f63e1772b2d chars:99",
            "passage": "10.1021-ja01629a058/p2/4",
            "source": "ex:msyn/source/10.1021-ja01629a058"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "locator": "p. 2",
            "note": "quote withheld: sha256:57a9b94004b6eb4fe92c8cbdb556ecbd4bbd9cc3337c853312bb4b9eb7a4e6eb chars:96",
            "passage": "10.1021-ja01629a058/p2/4",
            "source": "ex:msyn/source/10.1021-ja01629a058"
          }
        ],
        "inference_type": "theoretical",
        "statement": "The oxidation of the n-propyl alcohol may have yielded some acetic acid as well as propionic acid; if not removed in recrystallization, activity of its acid carbon would appear as activity of the 1-carbon of the propyl alcohol, while its methyl carbon would be discarded and not affect the results."
      }
    },
